#+TITLE: org-llm — user-defined MCP tools (Phase 23.6 — literate MCP tools)
#+AUTHOR: you
#+OPTIONS: toc:nil num:nil
#+FILETAGS: :org-llm:tools:literate-config:

# Copy this file to ~/org/org-llm-tools.org to enable. Override the
# location via the ORG_LLM_LITERATE_TOOLS_PATH env var. See
# docs/wiki/literate-tools.org for the full spec.
#
# Each top-level heading is ONE tool. The heading title becomes the
# Python function name; properties drawer carries metadata; the
# `#+begin_src python :tangle no` block is the function body. The
# org_llm.literate_mcp package compiles each into a sandboxed
# callable that the MCP server registers at startup.
#
# Required properties: :DESCRIPTION:, :PARAMS:.
# Optional:           :RETURNS:, :TIMEOUT:, :IMPORTS:, :DANGEROUS:.
#
# IMPORTS gates against a stdlib allowlist (json, re, math, datetime,
# collections, …). Modules outside the allowlist require BOTH
# :DANGEROUS: yes on the tool AND `dangerous_enabled=True` at the
# host's load-time. Two-key rule by design.

* word_count
:PROPERTIES:
:DESCRIPTION: Count whitespace-separated words in a string.
:PARAMS:      {"text": {"type": "string"}}
:RETURNS:     {"type": "integer"}
:END:

#+begin_src python :tangle no
return len(text.split())
#+end_src

* extract_urls
:PROPERTIES:
:DESCRIPTION: Pull every http(s) URL out of a blob of text.
:PARAMS:      {"text": {"type": "string"}}
:IMPORTS:     re
:END:

#+begin_src python :tangle no
return re.findall(r"https?://\S+", text)
#+end_src

* utc_now_iso
:PROPERTIES:
:DESCRIPTION: Return the current UTC time as an ISO-8601 string.
:PARAMS:      {}
:IMPORTS:     datetime
:END:

#+begin_src python :tangle no
return datetime.datetime.utcnow().isoformat() + "Z"
#+end_src
